---
intent: >
  Restructure provisionBrain from a 4-step pipeline (brain config →
  vault → playbook hub → vault CLAUDE.md → MCP) to a 5-step pipeline
  (brain config → brain root directories → playbook hub → research
  hub → MCP). Drop the vault-root CLAUDE.md scaffolding entirely.
  Drop every inline TypeScript hub-template constant; source hub
  artifact bytes from the parsed `playbookHub` and `researchHub`
  fields of the scaffolded brain.aide via parseBrainAide /
  parseBrainAideFromString. Rename every storage-specific identifier
  (vault, obsidian, hub note, wikilink, note) to storage-agnostic
  terms in code (function names, variable names, constants, JSDoc).
  The MCP step's prescription continues to derive from
  parseBrainAide + interpolateArgs as it does today.
---

## Project Structure

This is an edit plan against an existing module. The folder shape is
unchanged. The orchestrator's external signature stays the same. What
changes:

- The orchestrator returns 5 InitStep items instead of the current 5
  (the count is the same — the CLAUDE.md step is replaced by the
  research-hub step).
- The pipeline order shifts: step 4 was vault CLAUDE.md, step 4
  becomes Research hub.
- Hub-artifact step content is sourced from parsed brain.aide body
  sections, not inline constants.
- All storage-specific identifiers become storage-agnostic.

```
src/service/install/provisionBrain/
├── .aide                         ← [existing, aligned] intent spec — already
│                                    rewritten for the 5-step + storage-agnostic
│                                    + brain.aide-as-source-of-truth shape
├── plan.aide                     ← [this file, REPLACES the prior 7/7-done plan]
├── todo.aide                     ← [existing] alignment record (untouched)
├── index.ts                      ← [edit] orchestrator + helpers
│                                    export default async function provisionBrain(
│                                      projectRoot: string,
│                                      brainPath: string,
│                                      mcpConfigPath: string,
│                                    ): Promise<InitStep[]>
│                                    signature unchanged. Behavior changes:
│                                      - returns 5 InitStep items in NEW order:
│                                          1. Brain config (brain.aide)
│                                          2. Brain root directories
│                                          3. Playbook hub
│                                          4. Research hub
│                                          5. MCP config (brain)
│                                      - DROPS vault-root CLAUDE.md step entirely
│                                      - DROPS PLAYBOOK_HUB_TEMPLATE constant
│                                      - DROPS VAULT_CLAUDE_MD_TEMPLATE constant
│                                      - hub artifact steps source content from
│                                        parsed brain.aide body sections
│                                      - identifier renames (storage-agnostic):
│                                          vaultExists → brainRootExists
│                                          VAULT_DIRS → BRAIN_ROOT_DIRS
│                                          buildVaultStep → buildBrainRootStep
│                                          buildVaultClaudeMdStep → DELETED
│                                          buildPlaybookHubStep keeps its name
│                                          (already storage-agnostic) but its
│                                          content source moves
│                                          new helper: buildResearchHubStep
│                                          new helper: resolveBrainAideBody
│                                          (returns the parsed body sections
│                                          for the hub steps to read)
│                                      - JSDoc identifier sweep: no "vault",
│                                        "obsidian", "hub note", "wikilink",
│                                        "note" tokens remain in any code
│                                        identifier, comment, or constant
└── index.test.ts                 ← [edit] tests reflect the 5-step shape, the
                                     renames, and the brain.aide-sourced hub
                                     bytes; CLAUDE.md tests deleted, research
                                     hub tests added; storage-agnostic
                                     terminology in test names + descriptions
```

The helper subfolder `obsidianBrainAideTemplate/` is governed by its
own plan.aide (sibling) — this plan does NOT modify the template
helper's bytes; it consumes the template's output through
`parseBrainAideFromString`.

## Prerequisites

Two prerequisite plans must execute before this one. The orchestrator
runs prerequisite plans in dependency order; if either is missing,
this plan's tests will fail in diagnosable ways.

**1. `src/service/parseBrainAide/`** must export the widened
`ParseBrainAideResult.ok` shape AND the closed three-section body
grammar. Specifically:

- `parseBrainAideFromString(content)` returns `{ kind: "ok", config,
  prose, playbookHub, researchHub }` when the content carries
  exactly the three required sections.
- `parseBrainAide(root)` reads `.aide/config/brain.aide` and
  delegates to the same string parser.
- `interpolateArgs(config)` is a no-op on the default scaffold (no
  `${...}` placeholders) and substitutes any `${<key>}` against
  top-level frontmatter fields when present.

**2. `src/service/install/provisionBrain/obsidianBrainAideTemplate/`**
must emit a default brain.aide whose body carries all three required
sections (`## Prose`, `## Playbook hub`, `## Research hub`) and no
unknown top-level `## ` headings (nested headings inside any
section's body must be `### ` or deeper). Specifically:

- `obsidianBrainAideTemplate(rootPath: string): string` returns a
  string that round-trips through `parseBrainAideFromString` to
  `kind: "ok"`.
- The returned string's `## Playbook hub` body section, when
  extracted by the parser, equals the bytes the install service
  scaffolds as the playbook-hub artifact.
- The returned string's `## Research hub` body section, when
  extracted by the parser, equals the bytes the install service
  scaffolds as the research-hub artifact.

If `obsidianBrainAideTemplate`'s body widening has not landed when
this plan executes, every cold-install test that derives hub bytes
from the template will fail with `kind: "malformed-body"` (the
parser rejects the legacy single-section template). The orchestrator
must execute the template helper's plan before this plan's steps
run.

## Plan

### 1. Add `resolveBrainAideBody` helper for hub-byte sourcing

Read: `coding-playbook/architecture/data-flow`, `coding-playbook/foundations/conventions`

- [x] Edit `src/service/install/provisionBrain/index.ts`. Add a new
      private helper `resolveBrainAideBody` declared ABOVE
      `provisionBrain` (per the function-ordering rule) and ABOVE the
      step-builder helpers that consume it. Signature:

      ```
      async function resolveBrainAideBody(
        projectRoot: string,
        brainAideStep: InitStep,
      ): Promise<{ playbookHub: string; researchHub: string } | null>
      ```

      Behavior parallels the existing `resolveBrainAideConfig`
      helper but returns body sections instead of frontmatter:

      - When `brainAideStep.status === "would-create"` AND
        `brainAideStep.content` is defined, parse the in-memory
        template bytes via `parseBrainAideFromString`. This is the
        cold-install path where brain.aide has not hit disk yet.
      - Otherwise, parse the on-disk file via `parseBrainAide(projectRoot)`.
        This is the existing-brain.aide path.
      - On a successful parse (`kind === "ok"`), return
        `{ playbookHub: result.playbookHub, researchHub:
        result.researchHub }`.
      - On any non-ok result (`missing`, `malformed-frontmatter`,
        `malformed-body`), return `null`. The hub-artifact step
        builders fall back to a `would-skip` (or `would-create`
        with empty content) step in that case — the user must fix
        their brain.aide before the install can proceed.

      Update `resolveBrainAideConfig` (the existing helper) to share
      structure with the new helper if appropriate — both perform
      the same in-memory-vs-on-disk dispatch on the brain.aide step.
      Consider extracting a private utility that returns the full
      `ParseBrainAideResult` once and lets both helpers narrow on
      it. Optional refactor; if it complicates the code without
      eliminating duplication, leave the two helpers parallel.

      JSDoc requirements:
      - State that this helper is the SINGLE source of hub-artifact
        body bytes. The package no longer owns hub bytes as inline
        TypeScript constants; brain.aide is the authoritative
        source.
      - State that the in-memory cold-install path is structurally
        identical to the on-disk path: both round-trip through the
        same parser, both yield the same field shape.

### 2. Rename storage-specific identifiers and drop the CLAUDE.md helper

Read: `coding-playbook/foundations/conventions`, `coding-playbook/foundations/anti-patterns`

