        The function body's check on `.obsidian` directory
        presence is a storage-specific implementation detail —
        keep the check (it's a reasonable heuristic for "this
        directory looks already-provisioned") but isolate it in
        a comment that explicitly names the heuristic as
        Obsidian-flavored, not as a structural assumption. The
        function returns true when the directory is non-empty by
        any heuristic; an Obsidian-shaped brain returns true
        because of the `.obsidian` directory; a Notion-mounted
        brain returns true because of whatever non-empty file the
        Notion mount left there.
      - `VAULT_DIRS` → `BRAIN_ROOT_DIRS`. The constant value stays
        `["research", "process/retro", "coding-playbook"]` —
        these directory NAMES are part of the framework's brain
